IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgb1-s154-convicted-default`

-- Tests for sgb1-s154-convicted-default.l4 (Companies Act 1967, ss 154, 155, 155A; text lines 12393-12698 of CoA1967.txt).
-- Every expected value was written from the text of the Act, not from what the code printed; each group names the words it rests on.
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.


-- s 154(1): subject to the disqualifications "if (a) the person is convicted of ... (i) any offence ... involving fraud or dishonesty punishable with imprisonment for 3 months or more; (ii) any offence under Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001, where the conviction was on or after 1 July 2015; (iii) ... sections 50, 51, 53, 54, 55 or 55A of the CDSA, where the conviction is on or after the date of commencement of section 56 ...; or (b) ... civil penalty ... on or after 1 July 2015"
-- (a)(i): fraud or dishonesty, punishable with 3 months
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(i): punishable with only 2 months
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a)(i): punishable with 3 years
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` TRUE 36 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(ii): conviction on 1 July 2015
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE (Date 1 7 2015) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(ii): conviction on 30 June 2015
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE (Date 30 6 2015) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a)(iii): conviction on the commencement date
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(iii): conviction the day before commencement
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): civil penalty on 1 July 2015
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): civil penalty on 30 June 2015
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the limbs
#ASSERT `s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 154(2): "The court may, in addition to any other sentence imposed, make a disqualification order against any person who is convicted in Singapore of any of the following offences: (a) ... formation or management of a corporation; (b) section 157 or 396B; (c) section 237 or 239 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018"
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` TRUE `s 154(2)(a) an offence in connection with the formation or management of a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` TRUE `s 154(2)(b) an offence under section 157 or 396B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` TRUE `s 154(2)(c) an offence under section 237 or 239 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an offence not listed: the text lists, it does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` TRUE `s 154(2) some other offence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- convicted elsewhere than in Singapore: outside "convicted in Singapore"
#ASSERT `s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` FALSE `s 154(2)(a) an offence in connection with the formation or management of a corporation` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 154(8): "a District Court may make a disqualification order under this section"
#ASSERT `s 154(8) a District Court may make a disqualification order under the section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another court: the text names a District Court and says nothing of the rest
#ASSERT `s 154(8) a District Court may make a disqualification order under the section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 154(4): the disqualifications "(a) ... not sentenced to imprisonment -- take effect upon conviction and continue for a period of 5 years or for such shorter period as the court may order under subsection (2); (b) ... sentenced to imprisonment -- take effect upon conviction and continue for a period of 5 years after his or her release from prison; (c) ... civil penalty -- take effect upon the imposition ... and continue for a period of 5 years after the imposition"
-- (a): upon conviction
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date the disqualification takes effect` `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2026)
-- (b): upon conviction, not release
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date the disqualification takes effect` `s 154(4)(b) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) and sentenced to imprisonment` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2026)
-- (c): upon the imposition of the civil penalty
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date the disqualification takes effect` `s 154(4)(c) subject to the imposition of a civil penalty on or after 1 July 2015` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 7 2026)
-- (a): 5 years from the conviction
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the last day of the disqualification` `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS (Date 1 6 2031)
-- (a): a shorter period of 18 months ordered by the court
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the last day of the disqualification` `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE 18 EQUALS (Date 1 12 2027)
-- (b): 5 years after the release from prison
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the last day of the disqualification` `s 154(4)(b) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) and sentenced to imprisonment` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS (Date 1 6 2033)
-- (c): 5 years after the imposition of the civil penalty
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the last day of the disqualification` `s 154(4)(c) subject to the imposition of a civil penalty on or after 1 July 2015` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS (Date 1 7 2031)
-- the day the disqualification takes effect
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date asked is within the period of the disqualification` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2031) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the last day
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date asked is within the period of the disqualification` (Date 1 6 2031) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2031) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day after the last day
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date asked is within the period of the disqualification` (Date 2 6 2031) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day before it takes effect
#ASSERT `s 154(4) the date asked is within the period of the disqualification` (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 154(3): "Subject to any permission ..., a person who (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or (b) has had a disqualification order made ... must not act as a director, or take part ... in the management of a company, or of a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies, during the period of the disqualification"
-- (a), within the period, a company
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither (a) nor (b): outside "a person who"
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Subject to any permission": the Court gave permission
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- outside "during the period of the disqualification"
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a company or a Division 2 foreign company: the text names those
#ASSERT `s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 154(5): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 2 years or to both"
#ASSERT `s 154(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 154(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 154(5) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 154(5) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 154(5) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 154(6): "may apply to the Court for permission ... upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice of his or her intention to apply"
-- exactly 14 days
#ASSERT `s 154(6) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 13 days
#ASSERT `s 154(6) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a disqualified person: outside "A person who"
#ASSERT `s 154(6) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 154(7) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "On the hearing" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 154(7) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 155(2) and (5): a relevant requirement; a conviction under section 154(2)(a) is not treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement
-- a return, account or other document to be filed
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the provision is a relevant requirement of this Act for the purposes of the section` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- notice of any matter to be given to the Registrar
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the provision is a relevant requirement of this Act for the purposes of the section` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- other provisions: the text does not say
#ASSERT `s 155(2) the provision is a relevant requirement of this Act for the purposes of the section` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a flat negative
#ASSERT `s 155(5) the conviction is treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- other convictions: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 155(5) the conviction is treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155(8): "No account is to be taken ... of any offence which was committed or, in the case of a continuing offence, began before 15 May 1984"
-- the day before 15 May 1984
#ASSERT `s 155(8) account is taken of the offence for the purposes of the section` (Date 14 5 1984) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on that date the subsection says nothing more
#ASSERT `s 155(8) account is taken of the offence for the purposes of the section` (Date 15 5 1984) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155(4) and (3): three or more convictions, or three or more orders, within 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the person is treated as being adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences in relation to relevant requirements` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if the person is convicted of any 3 or more offences": 2 is not enough
#ASSERT `s 155(4) the person is treated as being adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences in relation to relevant requirements` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 offences
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the person's persistent default in relation to relevant requirements is conclusively proved` 3 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 3 orders
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the person's persistent default in relation to relevant requirements is conclusively proved` 0 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "may ... be conclusively proved by showing" 3 or more: otherwise the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 155(3) the person's persistent default in relation to relevant requirements is conclusively proved` 2 2 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155(1): "Where a person has been persistently in default ... and that person, within a period of 5 years after the person has last been adjudged guilty of any offence or has had made against the person an order under section 13 or 399 ..., without the permission of the Court, is a director or promoter of, or is in any way ... concerned ... in the management of a company, that person shall be guilty of an offence"
-- on the last day of the 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a day after the 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 2 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not persistently in default
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a director, promoter or concerned in the management
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- with the permission of the Court
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 155(1) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 155(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` FALSE (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155(6), (7), (9), (10), (11)
-- "nothing in this section is to be construed as preventing that person from complying with the order of the Court"
#ASSERT `s 155(6) the section prevents the person from complying with the order of the Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a third or subsequent order: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 155(6) the section prevents the person from complying with the order of the Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a certificate of the Registrar is received as prima facie evidence
#ASSERT `s 155(7) the certificate of the Registrar is received in all courts as prima facie evidence of the facts stated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 155(7) the certificate of the Registrar is received in all courts as prima facie evidence of the facts stated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- exactly 14 days' notice
#ASSERT `s 155(9) the person has given the Minister the notice the subsection requires` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 13 days' notice
#ASSERT `s 155(9) the person has given the Minister the notice the subsection requires` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 155(10) the Minister may be represented and may oppose the granting of the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "On the hearing" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 155(10) the Minister may be represented and may oppose the granting of the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "company includes an unregistered company"
#ASSERT `s 155(11) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes": the list is open
#ASSERT `s 155(11) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155A(1A): the period is (a) where the person had previously been disqualified, 5 years after the date on which the name of the last of the companies was struck off; (b) in any other case, 3 years after that date
-- (b): 3 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1A) the last day of the period of the disqualification` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2029)
-- (a): 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1A) the last day of the period of the disqualification` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2031)

-- s 155A(1): a person who had been a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years, and was a director of each when struck off, "must not act as director of, or ... take part in or be concerned in the management of, any company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies for the period specified in subsection (1A)"
-- on the last day of the 3 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 3 FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2029) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a day after the 3 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 3 FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2029) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- previously disqualified: 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 3 TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2029) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a day after the 5 years
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 3 TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2031) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only 2 companies struck off: outside "A person who"
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 2 FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a company or a Division 2 foreign company
#ASSERT `s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` 3 FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 155A(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 155A(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 155A(2) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 155A(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 155A(3): apply for permission to (a) the Registrar; or (b) the Court, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice; (3A): "An application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an application has been made to the Registrar ... and the decision ... is pending"
-- to the Registrar
#ASSERT `s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE `s 155A(3)(a) the Registrar` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- to the Court on exactly 14 days' notice
#ASSERT `s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE `s 155A(3)(b) the Court` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- to the Court on 13 days' notice
#ASSERT `s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE `s 155A(3)(b) the Court` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- subsection (3A): the Registrar's decision is pending
#ASSERT `s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` TRUE `s 155A(3)(b) the Court` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not subject to a disqualification: outside "A person who is subject to a disqualification"
#ASSERT `s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` FALSE `s 155A(3)(a) the Registrar` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "An application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an application has been made to the Registrar ... and the decision ... is pending"
#ASSERT `s 155A(3A) an application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no application pending: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 155A(3A) an application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(3B) the Registrar may grant the application under subsection (3)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "if" gate on a power: the grant ruling gives NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(3B) the Registrar may grant the application under subsection (3)(a)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(3C) the Court may grant the application under subsection (3)(b)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "if" gate on a power: the grant ruling gives NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(3C) the Court may grant the application under subsection (3)(b)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 155A(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "On the hearing" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 155A(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Regulative rules: each #TRACE has an EXPECT line above it naming the outcome the text gives; each rule has a breach trace where the text allows one.

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 154(3) a disqualified person must not act as a director or take part in the management of a company` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 154(3) act as a director, or take part in the management of a company, during the period of the disqualification` AT 9

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 154(3) a disqualified person must not act as a director or take part in the management of a company` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 9

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 155(1) a person persistently in default must not be a director or take part in the management of a company without permission` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 155(1) be a director or promoter of, or take part in the management of, a company without the permission of the Court, while persistently in default` AT 9

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 155(1) a person persistently in default must not be a director or take part in the management of a company without permission` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 9

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 155A(1) a person who was a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years must not act as a director` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 155A(1) act as a director of, or take part in the management of, a company during the period of the disqualification` AT 9

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 155A(1) a person who was a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years must not act as a director` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 9
